    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "config.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only bool_value. The body is one match. \"true\" | \"yes\" | \"on\" returns Ok(true). \"false\" | \"no\" | \"off\" returns Ok(false). Any other word returns Err(bad_value(key)). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not fold ASCII case. Do not touch editor_config_to_toml, width_value, trailing_value, or apply_document. The existing test yes_and_no_are_booleans stays green. The test on_and_off_are_booleans parses format_version = 1, document.indent_with_spaces = on, and document.ensure_trailing_newline = off. indent_with_spaces is true. ensure_trailing_newline is false. The same parser rejects document.indent_with_spaces = ON with ConfigError::BadValue for that key. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
  },
